that are failing, and that admitting it would undermine his bargain.","outcome":"He raises tolls sharply and orders the remaining Hollow routes closed, deepening the famine and forcing the Wardens and The Hollow into open opposition.","depends_on":["scn_the_enforcers_close_in"]},{"id":"scn_academy_council","title":"The Academy Council","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya brings Maris to argue before Academy cartographers and Wardens. The Wardens demand she bury her findings to protect the toll-funded repairs, while others want Kael exposed.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Persuade the council to act on the full truth about the failing bridges and the starving Hollow.","conflict":"Veya's refusal to admit error clashes with new evidence that her chart omitted a failing route, and the council splits over whether Kael is villain or saviour.","outcome":"Veya admits her mistake before the council. The council agrees to share the charts openly, but Kael has moved first and demands a meeting at the docks.","depends_on":["scn_kael_reads_the_chart"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Bargain","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_toll_gate_standoff","title":"The Toll Gate Standoff","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Veya, Maris, and Kael confront each other at the main toll gate as a skybridge begins to fail. Veya offers to share the charts openly if Kael eases the tolls on The Hollow.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want the tolls eased and the charts shared. Kael wants to keep control of the last stable routes.","conflict":"Kael equates price with worth and fears losing control. Veya has to trust a rival, and Maris has to forgive.","outcome":"Kael sees that his control would cost more than it gains. He accepts a bargain in which the charts guide repairs and Hollow grain crosses at reduced cost.","depends_on":["scn_academy_council"]},{"id":"scn_the_failing_span","title":"The Failing Span","summary":"A major span begins to collapse before the bargain takes effect. Veya reads the winds to find a safe window while Maris leads the grain haulers through the service corridors, and Kael opens the gates and spends his own ledgered stores on repairs.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get the grain haulers across and secure the span with Warden repairs before it fails.","conflict":"Time is short, Cartel guards doubt Kael's order, and the repairs cost him the wealth he equated with worth.","outcome":"The crossing succeeds and the span is shored up, but Kael loses his monopoly position and the Cartel turns against him.","depends_on":["scn_the_toll_gate_standoff"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What Remains","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_new_ledger","title":"The New Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel's anger and a reckoning. Tolls are rewritten so that wind-debt can be repaid in labour and grain as well as coin, funding repairs without starving the Hollow.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Settle a new toll arrangement that keeps the bridges repaired and The Hollow fed.","conflict":"Cartel princes resist the reduced tolls, and Wardens still distrust Kael after his sabotage of supplies.","outcome":"A reduced and shared toll system is adopted, but Kael is stripped of his post and left to answer for his past choices.","depends_on":["scn_the_failing_span"]},{"id":"scn_a_fed_hollow","title":"A Fed Hollow","summary":"In The Hollow, grain flows again and Maris tells the Hollow Circle what happened. She grapples with whether to forgive Kael and acknowledges that quiet work like hers also mattered.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Restore the Hollow's supply and settle Maris's loyalty to home and to Veya.","conflict":"Maris rarely forgives, and the Hollow's losses cannot be undone by a reduced toll.","outcome":"The Hollow is fed and Maris keeps her friendship with Veya, though she withholds forgiveness from Kael and the cost of the famine remains.","depends_on":["scn_the_new_ledger"]},{"id":"scn_charts_for_all","title":"Charts for All","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya publishes her charts openly, crediting Maris and her late mentor. She keeps tracking the drifting isles, accepting that some truths are safer shared than hoarded.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Share her charts and honour her mentor's theory.","conflict":"She wants recognition but must give credit away, and the isles are still drifting apart.","outcome":"The charts are shared across the archipelago, giving the isles a way to plan for the drift and leaving the question of Kael's legacy as both villain and saviour open.","depends_on":["scn_a_fed_hollow"]}]}]}
