 quietly asks to see her charts. She refuses to hand them over.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to check her chart against dock traffic. Kael wants her charts under Cartel control.","conflict":"Kael admires her skill but cannot let her succeed, and Veya fears becoming an ambitious power-seeker like him, yet will not yield.","outcome":"Veya keeps her charts but Kael learns the safe routes are few. He marks her as a threat to the Cartel's plans.","depends_on":["scn_charting_the_fade","scn_the_toll_ledger"]},{"id":"scn_maris_at_the_mill","title":"Grain in the Dark","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris sees the empty silos and the cost of the tolls. She begins planning to smuggle grain through service corridors that only she knows.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Secure enough grain to feed The Hollow through the crisis.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers watch the main routes, and Maris trusts few people with her secret paths.","outcome":"Maris plans her first smuggling run and decides she needs a navigator who understands the shifting bridges.","depends_on":["scn_the_toll_ledger"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Bridges Burning Thin","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_wardens_at_emberroost","title":"Cables of Cloudstone","summary":"Veya travels to Emberroost, where Bridge Wardens braid cables for the skybridges. They accuse Kael of sabotaging forge-island supplies, yet admit that the Cartel's tolls fund their repairs.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Learn whether the toll revenue truly keeps the bridges repaired and whether Kael is sabotaging supplies.","conflict":"The Wardens want her to publish the charts to damn Kael, but the same Wardens depend on his tolls to keep working, and Veya cannot bear to be wrong about him.","outcome":"Veya learns the tolls fund repairs while supplies to Emberroost are also being throttled, so Kael is both saviour and saboteur, and she sets out for The Hollow, where her routes cross the worst-hit bridges.","depends_on":["scn_rivals_at_the_docks"]},{"id":"scn_trading_paths","title":"Trading Paths","summary":"Veya reaches The Hollow and meets Maris. They trade wind-current knowledge for secret corridors, forming an alliance.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants a hidden route past Cartel watchers, and Maris wants a guide to the shifting bridges.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and fears that Veya's charts could expose her smuggling routes.","outcome":"They agree to exchange knowledge. Veya sees firsthand how the tolls are starving The Hollow, which shakes her view of the Wardens' cause.","depends_on":["scn_maris_at_the_mill","scn_wardens_at_emberroost"]},{"id":"scn_the_enforcers_close_in","title":"The Enforcers Close In","summary":"On a smuggling run along the service corridors, Cartel enforcers ambush Maris and Veya. They escape using Maris's pathfinding and Veya's reading of the winds, but some grain and a chart are lost.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Deliver grain to the Hollow's granaries without being caught.","conflict":"Enforcers have learned of the routes, and Veya's flame-free, cautious route still brings her into the open.","outcome":"The pair escape, but one of Veya's charts falls into Cartel hands and Maris must question whether Veya's presence endangers her people.","depends_on":["scn_trading_paths"]},{"id":"scn_kael_reads_the_chart","title":"Kael Reads the Chart","summary":"At Mistral Docks Kael studies the captured chart and recognises that Veya is right: most routes will fail. He moves to seize the last stable ones before the bridges collapse.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Turn the chart into Cartel control over the last stable skybridge routes.","conflict":"Kael sees that his monopoly rests on bridges that are failing, and that admitting it would undermine his bargain.","outcome":"He raises tolls sharply and orders the remaining Hollow routes closed, deepening the famine and forcing the Wardens and The Hollow into open opposition.","depends_on":["scn_the_enforcers_close_in"]},{"id":"scn_academy_council","title":"The Academy Council","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya brings Maris to argue before Academy cartographers and Wardens. The Wardens demand she bury her findings to protect the toll-funded repairs, while others want Kael exposed.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Persuade the council to act on the full truth about the failing bridges and the starving Hollow.","conflict":"Veya's refusal to admit error clashes with new evidence that her chart omitted a failing route, and the council splits over whether Kael is villain or saviour.","outcome":"Veya admits her mistake before the council. The council agrees to share the charts openly, but Kael has moved first and demands a meeting at the docks.","depends_on":["scn_kael_reads_the_chart"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Bargain","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_toll_gate_standoff","title":"The Toll Gate Standoff","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Veya, Maris, and Kael confront each other at the main toll gate as a skybridge begins to fail. Veya offers to share the charts openly if Kael eases the tolls on The Hollow.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want the tolls eased and the charts shared. Kael wants to keep control of the last stable routes.","conflict":"Kael equates price with worth and fears losing control. Veya has to trust a rival, and Maris has to forgive.","outcome":"Kael sees that his control would cost more than it gains. He accepts a bargain in which the charts guide repairs and Hollow grain crosses at reduced cost.","depends_on":["scn_academy_council"]},{"id":"scn_the_failing_span","title":"The Failing Span","summary":"A major span begins to collapse before the bargain takes effect. Veya reads the winds to find a safe window while Maris leads the grain haulers through the service corridors, and Kael opens the gates and spends his own ledgered stores on repairs.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get the grain haulers across and secure the span with Warden repairs before it fails.","conflict":"Time is short, Cartel guards doubt Kael's order, and the repairs cost him the wealth he equated with worth.","outcome":"The crossing succeeds and the span is shored up, but Kael loses his monopoly position and the Cartel turns against him.","depends_on":["scn_the_toll_gate_standoff"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What Remains","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_new_ledger","title":"The New Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel's anger and a reckoning. Tolls are rewritten so that wind-debt can be repaid in labour and grain as well as coin, funding repairs without starving the Hollow.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Settle a new toll arrangement that keeps the bridges repaired and The Hollow fed.","conflict":"Cartel princes resist the reduced tolls, and Wardens still distrust Kael after his sabotage of supplies.","outcome":"A reduced and shared toll system is adopted, but Kael is stripped of his post and left to answer for his past choices.","depends_on":["scn_the_failing_span"]},{"id":"scn_a_fed_hollow","title":"A Fed Hollow","summary":"In The Hollow, grain flows again and Maris tells the Hollow Circle what happened. She grapples with whether to forgive Kael and acknowledges that quiet work like hers also mattered.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Restore the Hollow's supply and settle Maris's loyalty to home and to Veya.","conflict":"Maris rarely forgives, and the Hollow's losses cannot be undone by a reduced toll.","outcome":"The Hollow is fed and Maris keeps her friendship with Veya, though she withholds forgiveness from Kael and the cost of the famine remains.","depends_on":["scn_the_new_ledger"]},{"id":"scn_charts_for_all","title":"Charts for All","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya publishes her charts openly, crediting Maris and her late mentor. She keeps tracking the drifting isles, accepting that some truths are safer shared than hoarded.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Share her charts and honour her mentor's theory.","conflict":"She wants recognition but must give credit away, and the isles are still drifting apart.","outcome":"The charts are shared across the archipelago, giving the isles a way to plan for the drift and leaving the question of Kael's legacy as both villain and saviour open.","depends_on":["scn_a_fed_hollow"]}]}]}
